From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32, sechost: protected credentials, best credential, domain credential writes

- CredProtect, CredUnprotect and CredIsProtected (A and W) were not
  exported (commented "@ stub"s). A credential string is protected for the
  user as DPAPI protects data (CryptProtectData, so another process of the
  same user, or the same user after a restart, can read it back, and no one
  else); the protected string is "@@D" and the blob in base64, so
  CredIsProtected tells CredUserProtection from CredUnprotected. The sizes
  are in characters with the terminating null; a short buffer is
  ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER with the size needed; an already protected or
  unprotected string comes back as it is.
- CredFindBestCredential (A and W): the credential of the target itself,
  else the most specific wildcard target ("*.example.com", then "*") of
  the type; ERROR_NOT_FOUND otherwise.
- CredWriteDomainCredentials (A and W): a domain credential written for the
  most specific name the target information has (DNS server name, NetBIOS
  server name, target, DNS domain, NetBIOS domain); not for other types.
- CredRename (A and W): ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED, as on Windows since Vista.
- sechost forwards them; wincred.h: CRED_PROTECTION_TYPE, the
  CRED_PACK_* and CREDUIWIN_* flags and the declarations.

Gate: test/credprotect-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/credprotect-probe.c).
Mutant SG_MUTANT_CRED_NOT_ENCRYPTED (advapi32/cred.c).
